## First-player playtest — Suggestions.md G2

Source: `Suggestions.md` G2 ("Watch five people play it") and
`docs/PLAYTEST.md`.

Every human acceptance test in `docs/PLAYTEST.md` was waived on 2026-09-28
(#324, #335), and none has been run. Waived means not owed, not passed: no bot
run can say whether the game is legible, moving, or boring at minute twelve.
`Suggestions.md` puts this first in its order of game work, because what five
people say should reorder everything after it.

Owner actions:

- Recruit five people who have not played or watched the game.
- Choose the build. The unsigned v0.1.0-beta.3 Windows installer (see #321
  above) is verified on a fresh VM but predates the Long Wait (#1794, #1797)
  and family challenges (#1796). To test what `main` plays now, cut a newer
  unsigned prerelease first (`.github/workflows/prerelease-tag.yml`, from an
  exact green `main` SHA).
- Give each person one Short Line with no editor, debug panel or explanation a
  normal player would not receive. Run `docs/PLAYTEST.md` as written, freeze
  the mechanisms it lists for the whole cohort, and fill in its per-participant
  record (build SHA, platform, campaign and actual years, seed, first or second
  run).
- Afterwards, ask the five questions in `Suggestions.md` G2: which three people
  they remember and why; what the house was trying to do; one decision that
  changed what happened later; what they weighed when choosing Record, Omit or
  Embellish; and where they stopped understanding what they were looking at.
- Record first, interpret second, tune last. Open each failed observation as a
  narrow new issue rather than reopening a waived one, and record the cohort
  report's date and location here.

Relevant docs: `docs/PLAYTEST.md` (protocol, per-participant record, cohort
report) and `Suggestions.md` §§4 (G2) and 7.
